# Styling & Design System

Visual tokens (ink, mint, fonts, motion, forbidden patterns) are owned by
`intelliroi-frontend-theme.mdc` and skill `intelliroi-theme` — do not redefine them here.

- Tailwind utility classes only; no inline `style={}` except for computed values (e.g. a
  chart's dynamic width) that genuinely can't be a class.
- All colors, spacing, and radii come from design tokens / CSS variables — no raw hex
  codes or magic pixel values in components.
- Status colors are semantic, not literal: use `success/warning/danger/info` tokens for
  budget health, ROI positive/negative, request status — never hardcode `text-red-500`
  when a semantic token exists.
- Use shadcn/ui primitives from `components/ui/` as the base for every new interactive
  element (Button, Dialog, Select, Table) — do not hand-roll a modal or dropdown.
- Charts (`components/charts/`) wrap recharts with project color tokens injected by
  default so every chart shares one palette without each usage re-specifying colors.
- Test every new component in light and dark themes before considering it done.
